1
00:00:03,600 --> 00:00:13,112
On January 22, 1970, the Boeing 747 made its first commercial flight, between New York and London, with Pan Am.

2
00:00:13,362 --> 00:00:20,810
It is called the jumbo jet: it can carry more than three hundred passengers, far more than the airliners of the time.

3
00:00:21,060 --> 00:00:27,044
Its distinctive hump houses an upper deck, which accommodated a lounge for passengers.

4
00:00:27,294 --> 00:00:33,374
The departure was, however, delayed: an engine problem forced the company to switch aircraft.

5
00:00:33,624 --> 00:00:40,376
Despite this false start, the 747 will open long-distance air travel to many more people.

6
00:00:40,626 --> 00:00:46,562
It will have flown for more than fifty years: the last delivery dates from 2023.

7
00:00:46,812 --> 00:00:50,996
File classified. Heading for space.
